---
import LegalDocument from '@/components/legal/legal-document.astro';
import PageIntro from '@/components/page-intro.astro';
import SubpageLayout from '@/layouts/subpage-layout.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'what-we-collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'how-we-use-it', title: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'ai', title: 'AI and your ChatGPT account' },
  { id: 'sharing', title: 'Who can see your trips' },
  { id: 'payments', title: 'Payments' },
  { id: 'your-choices', title: 'Your choices' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this page' }
];
---

<SubpageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Groam collects when you plan a trip, why, and the choices you have."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="Privacy"
    lede="What Groam collects when you plan a trip with us, why we need it, and the choices you have."
  />
  <LegalDocument toc={toc} updated="17 October 2026">
    <section id="what-we-collect">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        To run Groam we store what you put into it and what it needs to sign you in.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <b>Your account.</b> Your name, email address, and the sign-in details you set up,
          such as a password, a passkey, or two-step verification. We handle sign-in ourselves and keep your sessions so you stay signed in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Your groups.</b> The groups you create or join, their members, and the invitations
          you send.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Your trips.</b> Destinations, dates, itineraries, ideas, issues, and the
          conversations that sit next to them, including who wrote or changed what.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Files you add.</b> Photos and attachments you upload to a trip.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>AI activity.</b> The chats you have with Groam's AI agents and the results they
          produce in your trips.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="how-we-use-it">
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use this information to run the product: to show your group the shared plan,
        record every change on it, send the notifications you would expect, and keep your
        account secure. We do not need it for anything else, and this draft does not describe
        any other use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="ai">
      <h2>AI and your ChatGPT account</h2>
      <p>
        Groam's AI features run on your own connected ChatGPT account. When you ask an agent
        something, the relevant part of your trip and your message are sent to that service
        under your account, and the answer comes back into Groam. That service has its own
        terms and privacy policy, which apply to what it receives.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can connect or disconnect your account in your settings. Without a connection,
        you can still plan with your group.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="sharing">
      <h2>Who can see your trips</h2>
      <p>
        Trips belong to a group. Members of the group can see its trips, ideas, issues, and
        conversations, and can see who made each change. People outside the group cannot.
        Because Groam is built for planning together, anything you add to a shared trip is
        visible to the people you shared it with.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="payments">
      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Planning on your own is free. Inviting travelers will cost €1 per invited traveler,
        once. Paid invites are not live yet, so Groam is not collecting payment details
        today. When that changes, this page will be updated to say who handles payments and
        what they receive.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="your-choices">
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You can edit the details in your account and trips at any time.</li>
        <li>You can disconnect your ChatGPT account whenever you like.</li>
        <li>You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the information we hold about you.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        This is a draft. If we change it in a way that matters, we will update the date at the
        top of the page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalDocument>
</SubpageLayout>
